<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.2.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01754</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.2.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>c82ba93f-12a6-4a29-ac2b-b3906533b83d</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para><emphasis><emphasis>Students will complete the following questions to practice the skills they have learned in this lesson.</emphasis></emphasis></para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>Here are two patterns of dots.</item>
</list>
<para>Pattern A</para>
<para><figure><media alt="Four figures, labeled step 0 through 3. Step 0, no dots. Step 1, row of 4 dots. Step 2, 2 rows of 4 dots each. Step 3, 3 rows of 4 dots each."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/3c9a638d3d94a27279cdb7074d8c6646bb9233b2"/></media></figure></para>
<para>Pattern B</para>
<para><figure><media alt="Four figures, step 0 through 3. Step 0, 2 dots. Step 1 row of 1 dot above a row of 2 dots. Step 2, 2 rows of 2 dots each, above a row of 2 dots. Step 3, 3 rows of 3 dots each, above row of 2 dots."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/09162edcf5ac5e0e874b3d0a4bf64423e00003e7"/></media></figure></para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
    <item> How many dots will there be in Step 4 of Pattern A? </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 16</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
    <item> How many dots will there be in Step 4 of Pattern B? </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 18</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
    <item> Which pattern shows a quadratic relationship between the step number and the number of dots?
      <list>
        <item> Pattern A </item>
        <item> Pattern B </item>
      </list>
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Pattern B</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>Each expression represents the total number of dots in a pattern where \(n\) represents the step number.</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Select two</emphasis> expressions that represent a quadratic relationship between the step number and the total number of dots. (If you get stuck, consider sketching the first few steps of each pattern as described by the expression.)</para>

  <list>
    <item> \(n^2\) </item>
    <item> \(2n\) </item>
    <item> \(n \cdot n\) </item>
    <item> \(n+n\) </item>
    <item> \(n+2\) </item>
    <item> \(n \div 2\) </item>
  </list>

<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(n^2\) and \(n \cdot n\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item>Use the pattern below to answer the questions.</item>
</list>
<para><figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/951371a3b6b1037f7931fc4c9383339fea0673c6"/></media></figure></para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
    <item> How many blocks are in Step 4? </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 32</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
    <item> How many blocks are in Step 5? </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 44</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
    <item> How many blocks are in Step \(n\)?
      <list>
        <item> \(n^2-2\) </item>
        <item> \(n+6\) </item>
        <item> \((n+2)^2-n\) </item>
        <item> \((n+2)^2\) </item>
      </list>
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((n+2)^2-n\)</para></section>
</content>
